<title>USA: Cancer Treatment to buy back shares.</title>
<headline>Cancer Treatment to buy back shares.</headline>
<dateline>FORT LAUDERDALE, Fla. 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cancer Treatment Holdings Inc said its board of directors, which had previously authorized the buyback of up to 250,000 shares of its common stock, intends to activate its buyback program beginning April 25, 1997.</p>
<p>Under this authorization, the purchases may be made on the open market or through private transactions.  </p>
<p>The company currently has about 3.3 million shares outstanding.</p>
</text>
